{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the equation \\(x\\sqrt{x} - 5x - 9\\sqrt{x} = 35\\), we start by letting \\(y = \\sqrt{x}\\). This implies that \\(y^2 = x\\). Substituting \\(y\\) into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[y^3 - 5y^2 - 9y = 35.\\]\n\nWe need to find integer values of \\(y\\) that satisfy this equation. We can test possible integer values for \\(y\\):\n\n1. If \\(y = 5\\):\n   \\[5^3 - 5 \\cdot 5^2 - 9 \\cdot 5 = 125 - 125 - 45 = -45 \\neq 35.\\]\n   So, \\(y = 5\\) is not a solution.\n\n2. If \\(y = 6\\):\n   \\[6^3 - 5 \\cdot 6^2 - 9 \\cdot 6 = 216 - 180 - 54 = -18 \\neq 35.\\]\n   So, \\(y = 6\\) is not a solution.\n\n","prefix_end":564,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,23606,17767,87,59,26888,45340,92,481,220,20,87,481,220,24,59,26888,45340,92,284,220,18,20,59,701,582,1191,553,20194,17767,88,284,1124,26888,45340,11035,568,1096,23945,429,17767,88,61,17,284,856,59,568,3719,3696,10607,17767,88,57758,1119,279,23606,11,582,633,1447,78045,88,61,18,481,220,20,88,61,17,481,220,24,88,284,220,18,20,7110,2533,1654,1184,311,1477,7546,2750,315,17767,88,57758,429,26553,419,23606,13,1205,646,1273,3204,7546,2750,369,17767,88,59,7731,16,13,1416,17767,88,284,220,20,59,982,256,1124,58,20,61,18,481,220,20,1124,50853,220,20,61,17,481,220,24,1124,50853,220,20,284,220,16,17,20,481,220,16,17,20,481,220,19,20,284,481,19,20,1124,811,80,220,18,20,7110,921,256,2055,11,17767,88,284,220,20,57758,374,537,264,6291,382,17,13,1416,17767,88,284,220,21,59,982,256,1124,58,21,61,18,481,220,20,1124,50853,220,21,61,17,481,220,24,1124,50853,220,21,284,220,17,16,21,481,220,16,23,15,481,220,20,19,284,481,16,23,1124,811,80,220,18,20,7110,921,256,2055,11,17767,88,284,220,21,57758,374,537,264,6291,382,18,13,1416,17767,88,284,220,22,59,982,256,1124,58,22,61,18,481,220,20,1124,50853,220,22,61,17,481,220,24,1124,50853,220,22,284,220,18,19,18,481,220,17,19,